{
  "@@locale": "en",
  "@@x-translator-notes": "Wortschatz is a game-style app for learning German vocabulary: flashcards, spelling practice and three word games (Hive, Der Die Das, Fallee). The user is learning German; this text is the app's UI in the user's own language. Tone: warm, short, upbeat, casual; address the user informally where the language allows (du/tu/ты...). Never translate German learning content: German words, the articles der/die/das, German example sentences, and the German words in quotes such as 'Richtig!' stay exactly as given. Keep the brand 'Wortschatz' and the game names 'Hive', 'Der Die Das' and 'Fallee' in Latin letters, unchanged. Keep emoji and {placeholders} exactly. Use Latin digits. 'Arcade' must never become a word for a gambling or slot-machine hall. Most strings sit on buttons, chips or one-line rows on a 360 dp wide phone: prefer short words. Strings in ALL CAPS in English are shown in capitals: write them in capitals too if your script has them, with your language's own casing rules (Turkish i → İ, German ß stays ß); scripts without capitals just write the text.",
